You can implement the Fibonacci function in Rust using recursion without any additional packages. Here's a simple example:
```rust
fn fibonacci(n: u32) -> u32 {
    if n <= 1 {
        n
    } else {
        fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2)
    }
}
```
This function uses recursion to calculate the Fibonacci number. It's a direct translation of the mathematical definition and works well for small values of `n`.
